# Use Documentation MCP for Library Docs

When you need to see **any documentation** (libraries, APIs, frameworks, packages), use the **user-context7** MCP server to retrieve up-to-date docs and code examples instead of relying only on built-in knowledge or web search.

## When to use

- Looking up library/framework API (React, Vue, TypeScript, etc.)
- Checking package usage, options, or examples
- Verifying current docs for a dependency
- Need official or up-to-date code samples

## How to use

1. Use MCP tools from the **user-context7** server (e.g. list/read tool descriptors in `mcps/user-context7/` if needed).
2. Call the appropriate tool to fetch documentation for the library or topic in question.
3. Prefer this over guessing from memory when accuracy or recency matters.

## Note

"contact7" in project discussions refers to this documentation MCP (user-context7). Always prefer it when the task involves reading or following documentation.
